>instances to run on same hardware without VM running).

That's an LPAR. I believe it is more like Sun's E10000 scheme, except that
IBM's method is atomic to the extent that one can dedicate percentages of
a single CPU between partitions. Your OS/2 workstation [the master
console; it has some funny name] functions somewhat like the E10000's SSP
in its ability to shift resources between the system images.

I'm pretty sure that one LPAR can't dynamically request more resources for
itself - the request must come from the master console.


