Alan,

Consider DSL of one typ or another. Rent 2 (a)dsl devices and get a 4
wire dry coper line point to point for the the rboc (tell them it is
an alarm circuit...this is important.) If your rates ar similar to
Southwestern bell it will run you ~$80 for the alarm circuit/mo and
about $200 to $300 for the rental/lease of the (a)dsl equip. You will
get at the basic rate 384Kb up and 768Kb down to a theoretical max
(equipment counts here) of 8Mb . 

http://www.whatis.com/dsl.htm

Yes I know that DSL is "budding" technology but the DSL devices have
been around quitly for a couple of years. The fact that your LEC is
the same for both building makes this pretty atractive.

I personally would not recomend a T1 option unless you choose a point
to point solution. And this will often incure Local loop fees. There
are several deviceses that could make T1 posible over dry copper
(Adtran has a TSU that can front end a t1 router/bridge) but the set
up time and equipment cost are slightly higher (t1 = 1.5Kb up/down)

Happy bandwidth hunting....

