Hello,

I have a DCNT cluster. It's running NT 4.0 SP3 and DCNT 1.1 SP3.
One of the systems is misbehaving. For the purposes of this
post, let's call the two systems A and B and the cluster alias
CLUSTER.

When system A is primary (i.e., has access to the shared
RAID storage device), it happily serves the CLUSTER alias. 
When browsing the network, there is a listing for CLUSTER 
and it serves the share on the RAID device. There is also
an Oracle7 failover object. A named pipe pointing to host
CLUSTER correctly resolves to system A as well.

