Hmmm, we've circled back into the point I keep seeing JF raise: nobody
starts out with small VMS systems, which by virtue of things like SMP
and clustering *can* scale to enormous sizes fairly easily.  So by
losing the entire low end, VMS loses the foot in the door for most of
the systems that grow to be in the high end.  (Not that I have a
solution to that issue, but I do know from experience that VMS can be a
good part of a strategy to handling an application that might grow at
astonishing rates).

I still think someone who's *really* on the ball would choose their
technology to minimize the pain of finding themselves on a rocketing
growth curve.  But maybe that's just me!

Duncan



