Do not confuse "Wolf Pack" (now called Microsoft Cluster Software - MSCS);
with Nonstop Software for Windows NT Clusters, which supports the same
fail-over, and TP APIs we have on NSK. MSCS is Stone Age.

AIUI, The current max Tandem NT cluster is 24 cpus. That is 6, 4-way SMP
Compaq Prolient 5500s using ServerNet (which can include Himalayas on the
same Server Area Network).

The first cluster I recall was a CS-150: 2, 2-way SMP with only MSCS for
cluster control, and a fragile internal RAID-1.  It was quickly turned into
a table.






