In article <sjCd3.18235$ga.27882@news21.bellglobal.com>, "Jim Dew" <mountaindew@sympatico.ca> writes:
:I know through decus you can get a hobyest liscense for vms, is there
:anything like this for digitals unix?

  No, not at present.

  Also, the current generation Compaq Tru64 Unix does not support VAX 
  -- it presently operates only on Alpha systems, and I am aware of no
  plans to (ever) port it to VAX.

  The older ULTRIX operating system did support specific VAX systems,
  but was primarily targeted at the MIPS platform.

  You might find a NetBSD or Linux port around for VAX -- I know that
  there have been ports for various VAX systems.

  The OpenVMS Hobbyist license, information and media (circa US$30) are 
  available via:

    http://www.montagar.com/hobbyist/

 -------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
