In article <3769F1C4.70BCD348@bph.krakow.pl>, =?iso-8859-2?Q?Pawe=B3?= Kmiecik <p.kmiecik@bph.krakow.pl> writes:
:I have one important question about OVMS ver 7.2 
:I would like to know if this version supports XMI architecture?

  What is the question behind this question?  Why do you ask?  Problems?

  OpenVMS generally does not explicitly document support at the bus level, 
  but does tend to document the support of specific devices as part of the 
  Software Product Description (SPD) -- various XMI devices included.

  That said, the XMI bus is key to a variety of VAX and Alpha platforms, 
  and a large number of large OpenVMS systems would not function without 
  a functioning XMI bus -- the VAX 6000, VAX 7000, DEC 7000 and various 
  other systems all use the XMI and depend on various XMI widgets, and 
  all these systems are supported by OpenVMS V7.2.

  There are no plans to remove XMI support from OpenVMS.

 -------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
