In article <376c702f.8842192@news1.sympatico.ca>, mountaindew@earthling.net (Jim Dew) writes:
:I built the console cable that is supposed to let me access the
:console of the uvaxII, however i am dont get any data through the
:cable when i connect it to a pc. i have the pc software set to XON /
:XOFF flow control.

  Get rid of the PC and get a real terminal -- using the PC here adds 
  another layer of complexity to the problem, and complexity is not 
  something you want when you are troubleshooting hardware...

  See the OpenVMS Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) for information
  on the console panel, and the DB9 console pinout and cabling:

    http://www.openvms.digital.com/

:i launched the terminal, set it up, and then powerd up the uvaxII. it
:beeps once, but the led counts to A no problem.. however it seems to
:be too fast, like it is skipping some numbers or something

  How far does it get?  Just to A?  If so, it appears you have
  problems with the graphics controller or with the Q-bus -- the
  counter should count down to somewhere around 3 to 0, depending
  on the accessability of the operating system disk...

  Please see previous discussions with the word "serpentine" posted
  here or in comp.os.vms by myself or others -- these tend to be
  discussions of how to set up the Q-bus on one of these systems.

:i have all the buttons on the front of the case in the out position

  As a first step, remove all cards from the Q-bus save for the
  CPU and memory, and see how far you get.  (Remember which slots
  you removed the cards from and -- obviously -- remember to have
  the system powered down and to take full anti-static precautions
  before/when handling Q-bus modules.

