You left out:

Most customers buying linux know what they want and how they want it
and regardless of what you do they are going to redo it anyways.

We get boxes with Tru64 Unix installed on them here and basically,
wipe them and reinstall to fix how we like it.  

I've even heard of sites with NT doing the same thing.  When I worked
as a Sys Admin in a former life, we would boot up the sun/hp/whatever
and do a reload over the network.  The issue was, there was no way
that it was going to come configured in such a way that it would work
in our enviroment.

So, we basically just blew away the installation and through on a new
one through the network that did what we wanted it to.

