If it doesn't do Ethernet *bridging*, however, it won't work with LAT.

It might be possible to make Linux do that, but I don't think it would be
particularly easy -- I don't believe its PPP has support for any protocol
you can just dump raw Ethernet frames in, nor is there any kind of
"learning bridge" functionality AFAIK.

If ISDN gear will do, one of the cheaper Ascend Pipelines would work
great, even the old bridging-only models like the P50.  If it won't,
I *think* (but don't quite remember) the older Livingston Portmasters
might do the trick -- they can dial tens of modems at once, too, if
necessary, to give higher aggregate bandwidth.

