It is often stated in the newsgroups that Compaq doesn't get much from selling
a PC running NT or Windows since the royalties for the software all go to
Microsoft, and when they sell VMS, Compaq makes more money.

What puzzles me right now are those HP ads "HP servers running unstoppable NT"
with the kung-fu fighters.

Does Microsoft pay for those ads or does HP provide free advertising for
Microsoft products ?
And why would HP provide such free advertising which does absolutely nothing
to describe why HP hardware is better than any other that runs NT ?

If Microsoft starts to require free advertising from OEMs such as HP, can we
expect that out of Compaq ? Would this not mean that Compaq's advertising of
VMS and NSK and UNIX would have to be severely curtailed ?

If Compaq is forced by Billy to start making claims that NT is unstoppable,
how will this affect Compaq's supposed strategy of pushing VMS and NSK at
mission critical "unstoppable" customers ?



