Now Posted)...

Sorry to start a new thread here, just a l'il argument with Netscape
Negotiator...

Regarding the Windoze NT Cluster File System, which I believe I
referenced in my DECUS presentation, here's what I know:

DIGITAL engineers in Scotland developed a cluster file system for NT.
It's safe to assume that they borrowed heavily from extant OVMS
knowledge.

The aforementioned CFS, as well as the complementary distributed lock
manager, were remanded unto the custody of Micro$oft in September 1998.
Why? Heck, I dunno! Perhaps CPQ can come up with a plausible explanation
for this instantiation of a technology divestiture. I certainly cannot.

To the best of my knowledge, this technology has not yet been released
on the unsuspecting public. But for what it's worth, a senior Tandem
person stated that the joint CPQ/Micro$oft effort to imbue NT with "Sumo
Wrestler" characteristics (thanks, HP!) is focused on the file system.

And as Hoff mentioned, this work has precious little to do with the
technology frequently referred to as Dollar, TNFS, or Spiralog.

