"D.Webb" wrote:
> A VMS cluster can be configured with a cluster alias. All connections goto the
> cluster alias and then are directed to the least loaded system in the cluster.

Fine and dandy. But how is the cluster-alias imlemented in terms of
availability ? Isn't there a single system which handles the load-balancing to
direct incoming transasctions to the least loaded system ? Or is that
implemented in a single router ?

Sounds like a possible single point of failure to me.

That is why, in the good old VAX days, Digital (remember them ?) had the
VAXFT. a fault tolerant small front end to direct transactions to an available
processing node.

Come to think of it, it might be wise for Compaq to pitch the following config:

A tandem fault tolerant front end acting as the router to direct transactions
to a VMS cluster.



