Michael Duebner <michael@ics911.com> writes:
> I am trying to locate the AXP version of VMS 6.2.  I have two condist sets,
> one from December 1995 and another from March 1996.  In checking the
> documentation that accompanied the media, it made no mention as to the
> version of VMS that is on it.

  What do you mean by "condist"? There are 3 separate things, which can be
ordered separately or together:

  1) The VMS distribution CD's
  2) The layered product distribution CD's
  3) The layered product documentation CD's

  The combined thing is called "LPOS" (Layered Products and Operating System).
For part numbers, consult the VMS SPD on www.openvms.digital.com.

> 1) How can I find out what is included with the sets?

  Each of the above items should include a Bill of Materials (BOM), printed
on 8.5x11 paper in Courier, listing the part numbers of each item in the kit.

> 2) What sources are there for VMS 6.2 for the Alpha?

  In the old days, you could place an order for an "archival version", which
you did by asking the DECdirect person to add a "notes" field saying "must
ship archival kit version 6.2". Then you'd get the regular current shipping
kit, call and complain, and they'd give you and RMA and get it right the sec-
ond time. I don't know if this still works.

  You could also get a letter from an authorized DEC rep giving a 3rd party
permission to make their kit available to you. I don't know if that works,
either.

  Why do you have a specific need for 6.2, as opposed to either some other
version you have, or the current versions (V7.1-x, V7.2)?

