I totally agree.  What I neglected to mention earlier is that Tandem
users do not use the machines because of "Brand Name Loyalty."
We use them for reliability and continuous availability. Even so, I
would not mind having a small used CLX in my den ;-)

I am located at a call center and the Himalays are very good at CTI
especially when large volumes of calls are the order of the day.  The
application(s) we use have been fine tuned and all processors are
managing equal loads.  The load accross disk volumes is fairly equal.

Installation of another product and even som IPMs takes planning to
insure that there will be no impact on system performance.  Large
shops usually have the advantage of multiple systems and deveopment
boxes where they will take the time to test the new IPMs thouroghly
before installing them on the production boxes.  

The software vendor, if a third party product, will want to test the
software with the new IPMs before you place it on your system.
This is the other reason I have delayed my D48 install.  We need to
test our current software with D48 prior to the install and a few
weeks after that the Y2K compliant version of our software will be
installed on the D48 system.  So in this case the vendor has to test
twice.


