Dave Greenwood (greenwoodde@feda01.fed.ornl.gov) wrote:
: I just received a PW500AU workstation, but it doesn't have a graphics
: card.  Until the card arrives I was hoping to use a vt220 (lookalike)
: as a console.  I tried hooking it up to both COM ports and tried a
: couple of different baud rates, but so far nothing has shown up on
: the screen.
: 
: Assuming I can use a vt220 as a console on that workstation, can (will)
: someone tell me the settings I need to use?

Note that the 9-pin serial connector on the 500 is the PC standard, not the
old DEC standard (which, by the way, preceded the PC standard), so make sure
you're using the proper connections.  You'll need a null-modem between the 500
and the VT220.  The baud rate is 9600, with no parity, 8 bits.

Also, if you have a keyboard plugged into the 500, take it out.  The keyboard,
or lack thereof, is how the console determines where it should send output.
If you have a keyboard plugged in, then it may not talk to the serial at all.

        Stu



