re: responsability of patches.

While on my bike today, I got to think about this.

Good communications between the IT supplier and the customer is what is
critical to ensuring that patches are installed when/of needed (or that they
are available).  A good user group is also crucial in informing customers of
potential problems experienced by others (or telling them that installing a
certain patch is not going to cause problems).

When you think about it, the big difference between "enterprise" and
"PC-nintendo" systems is the fact that for enterprise systems, you expect to
have a communications path to the company.



