Hello.

Recently I attempted to reboot our 433au Alpha system running OSF/1
4.0 and failed.  After powerup the disks spin up and make a repetitive
noise but the boot fails and there is not even a video signal.

I found that I can remove the NVRAM/clock battery for a moment and
upon powerup, this will allow me to get to at least the AlphaBIOS.  I
then set the entries in CMOS to boot Unix (SRM) and then power down
for the proscribed 45 seconds.  However, on power up I am back were I
started, no boot, no video, etc.

I read on dejanews that maybe the battery needs replacing or that
there is faulty contact with the battery.  I have replaced the battery
and have assured that the leads make a good contact by bending the top
and bottom leads slightly to provide more force.  All to no avail.

Does anyone have any ideas?  If I do not give enough info, please tell
me and I will supply it.

