In article <37683B09.9D9D9238@ins-msi.com>, Jeff Campbell <jcampbell@ins-msi.com> wrote:
>On powerup the console displays:
>
>        ?? 003 3  DZ 0112
>
>When I type "SH ER" I see:
>
>        ?? 003 3  DZ 0070
>        003 000A 00000071 00008120 00001CC8 00000001 00000000 000000A0
>

03 DZ is the serial line controller (which controls the mouse, keyboard, 
printer port/alternate console and the other port (TTA2?).

The 003 part is the FRU (field replaceable unit) which in this case is the 
mouse. The others are:
        001             - system board
        002             - keyboard
        004             - monitor #1
        005             - monitor #2
        010-019       - graphics boards
        020-029       - COMM boards
        030-039       - bus adapters
        040-049       - memory (040 = SIMM #1, 041 = SIMM #2 etc.)
        100-199       - SCSI controller

Appendix G gives more information about this failure (0112):

"You are running tests and using the round mouse. Disregard this message the 
mouse is fine"

Don't ask me ... I'm just quoting the book!

