Have you ever been inside a solar cell manufacturing plant?
Black aluminum dust *everywhere*.  A local company uses 11/23's on the
production floor to run some custom instruments, and every card
inside was covered with an eighth of an inch of aluminum dust.
Yet - the machine still works!

As I understand it, most black metallic dusts are oxidized and
non-conductive.  It's the only way to explain how machines work
in such environments.

Tim.



