First off, there is no power switch, that's the reset breaker on the
power supply.  The red button restores default settings if held in
during poweron.  The LEDs show status.

A DECserver 200 requires a host to download the control file (usually
PR0801ENG.SYS, from the VMS layered products distribution).  You will
need a host that uses DECnet and supports the MOP download maintenance
protocol.  Also, the DECserver does not use TCP/IP or Telnet.  It uses
LAT, a proprietary DEC network protocol.  I don't recall that an HP3000
ever supported LAT or DECnet, maybe KI Research provided a 3rd party
program for this?

Chance are you have a mostly useless terminal server for an HP.
          Jack Peacock




