Rich Lafferty <rich@vax2.concordia.ca> wrote:
>Peter da Silva <peter@baileynm.com> wrote:
>> Due to a PC rollout so the users can convert to Lotus Notes, we will soon
>> have about 40-50 surplus VTX2000s, with whatever of their VRC16 monitors
>> don't play nice with the new PCs, as well as 5 or 6 Infoserver 1000s to
>> boot from, all with keyboards and mice.

>Peter, for the hobbyists and non-model-number-literate amongst us
>(like, oh, say, me) what are these? :-)

VXT2000 is a DEC X-terminal. It boots and loads files from the Infoservers,
so you need an Infoserver (or something that'll look like one) to use it.
The VRC16 is a nominal-17", 16" viewable, monitor. It's a multisync, but
only just, and we would be unloading the ones we can't convince to work on
a PC.

