> dies.  I'm assuming this is a power supply problem.

  Most likely cause is a fan failure, but there are microswitches on the
  covers so if you remove the covers to look at the fans it will not power
  up anyway.
  Perhaps you could open the machine up and inspect the fans to see if
  one is stiff to turn, or test the fans in some other way.
  (If the machine 'sees' that a fan or fans are not turning, it powers
  itself off again within a second or two).
 
  Hope this helps,
 
  Brian
 
 




