    20 years ago, computer room cleaning was mandatory.  You had large open
tape drives and mountable disk.  9 Track tapes are not as common and no one
uses open mountable disk anymore.
    Although it is not as important, computer room still need to be kept
clean, but not to clean room standards.  Lab jackets are nice, but class
100,000 clean room standards are not needed.
    Floors need to be dust mopped daily and "dry" wet mopped weekly by a
professional janitorial service.  Operators need to dust and clean monitors
as necessary.  Your Field Engineer should vacuum out systems and should
vacuum or replace on a regular basis  filters.  Tape drives should be
cleaned weekly or every 20 tapes.  High speed line printers (600lpm+)
should be vacuumed each ribbon change.




