On Tue, 08 Jun 1999 04:57:31 GMT, "Matt Goss" <matt@asdfkjl.om> wrote:


>I have a Digital Celebris SP90 and I am looking for information on it.  The
>Compaq site does not have the information.  I am looking for RAM
>configuration, chip upgradability, etc.

I assume this is a Celebris FP590 - right?  There was no "SP90".

RAM: 70ns standard (FPM) SIMMs, parity or non-parity supported.  EDO
not supported.  There are four slots and you could put 64MB SIMMs in
each slot if you like.  Unlike many Pentium systems, you can have just
one SIMM in a bank (slot 0 or 2), but performance will suffer a bit.
The system can be configured with either 256K or 512K cache - this is
not a "standard" part, so is not easily replaceable.

CPU: it is a "Socket 5" system with a 3.3V regulator.  If you want to
go above 133MHz, you'll need an "OverDrive" chip.  I think a 200MMX
OverDrive will work - I had a 166(non-MMX) in mine.  Jumpers on the
board select clock input (50MHz, 60MHz or 66MHz).  There is no clock
multiplier jumper.  I have no idea how any of the non-Intel CPU
upgrades would work with it.

A well-designed workhorse of a system.



