Hmm. The PSU comes in a number of lumps, consisting of the PSU chassis,
containing the mains transformer and +15v supply and AC line monitoring
bits (this overall lump is I think the H742), and a collection of plug-
in regulator modules, which generate the other voltages required by the
CPU and Unibus devices. These modules have numbers along the lines of
H754 or H745. I seem to remember that a /40 requires 3 +5v modules,
a -15v module, and a +20/-5v modules (for the core memory). So those
are the bits you need to shop for. Does you machine have the PSU harness
(big loom of cables that connects the CPU box to the PSU)? Getting one 
as a spare part may be a bit of a challenge...

The KM11 is a maintenance option, used for single-stepping the microcode
and so forth. Although it's useful to have, it's not essential. 

James

