No, No,  DECUS is a Greek word.  It has a somewhat long and complex meaning.
I'll do my best to explain it's meaning in as little textual space as possible.


Little Known Greek Mythology:

Long long ago in Silicus a heavenly land occupied by the gods, there came to be
four powerful or influential god-beings:  Pee-Pee-Cus,  Mipus, Intecus, and Decus.
They were the most powerful of all the gods in Silicus.  Pee-Pee-Cus' was
called into existence by two naturally occurring power poles called Inter Bellus
Motorolium which existed only as a result of their relation one to the other.
Pee-Pee-Cus was worshipped by a race of artisians that called them selves
Max Toshers.  They were truly PINK; unobtrusive know-nots but generally
peaceful and content in their existence worshipping their god Pee-Pee-Cus.
It was the worship of Max Toshers that gave Pee-Pee-Cus his power.  There was
another group called Amigotians that worshipped this god but Pee-Pee-Cus
favored them not and discouraged their proliferation but that is another
story in Silicus history so I will not elaborate further on them nor the
plights of their existence.

Mipus was a very colorful god that expressed himself in beautiful shades and
hues such as indigo and onyx.  This god had many fine and noble qualities.  He
had a soft heart though reality based, but was very demanding and taxed his
followers into submission.  His following therefore was not actively growing
and as a result the influence of Mipus in the land of Silicus was limited.

Decus the subject of this tale true, was by far the most powerful god in the
land and was especially known for his great speed and breadth of ability.
He was revered by all the other gods which held him in the highest revere.
Among the gods Decus was referred to as Alphas meaning: the first one, the
great one, numero uno.  His following was unsolicited and they were among
the wisest beings in existence. Self thinking and independent without
prejudice they banded together not in mindless worship of a dead and useless
god but promoted individualism and betterment of any who would join in
the tributing of the living Decus.

Intecus was an introvert a demigod really, and had become weak from spending
the first half of his existence in deep morose masturbation.  One day he
looked up from his self-involved introversion and noticed the other gods
laughing at him because his following were all chronic masturbaters as was
he himself was.  He sought to avenge his name creating evil among the
followers of the other gods.  From the bowels of scum itself he scraped
together the ooze that would become his vehicle for the delivery of chaos.
As the formless slime took shape he gave his creation name.  A dark
whisper at first  "eghm esss daughsss".  The slime grew among the beings
that followed their gods and stole their minds and corrupted their harts.
The first movements of this monster did not go unnoticed however as it
took by force the Community Pro Mutuality known to all fair of hart
simply as CPM.   This almost caused the scummy evil monster to be seen
in a light that would reveal the will of Intecus and so Intecus was forced
to unfold his discord on the unsuspecting ever so more slowly and took
greater caution in his scheming.   He spun many lies and conjured many
illusions in order to deceive those that he may in preparation for the blows
of his revenge to come.   He diverted the credit for the achievements and
goodness of the other gods to himself while delivering the blame and fault
for his dastardly deeds unto the other gods.

His plans were advanced greatly by an evil one among the innocent.  The evil
one took to recruiting all the stupid and mindless by promoting the lies
spun by eghm esss daughsss and Intecus.  The evil one grew in popularity
for the stupid and mindless were many.  In flocks and groves they came to
worship the slime through the evil one.  He became known to them as
Beel Gateus and the method of witless worship he wheeled was known as
"my-crow-soft" and was the long prophesied anti-decus incarnate.  Together
this unholy trio campaigned intensely the my-crow-soft way and embodied
all that was slow.  This was the chief sign that convinced those who could
still think for themselves and the fair of heart that the anti-decus had
indeed come.

Well to make a long story longer, all the other gods fell in the face of
this intense chaotic evil unprepared, and unready for such an onslaught
carried out by the stupid and the mindless.   Decus was the last to fall
and was finally defeated by an infiltration of the stupid into the upper
ranks of those who organized and managed his followers.

Down through time as this story was told generation to generation, father
to son the word DECUS came to mean:

        Greatness managed by the stupid soon falls



