Steven,

Absolutely for sure, you can change a pair of jumpers on the processor
card, and install up to a Pentium 133.

If the processor card is DEC part number 54-24490-01, it will support
up to a Pentium 200 with the right voltage regulator attached.  Not
the one on the CPU card right now, but a different one.

Either CPU card is capable of running a dual processor, as long as the
CPU steppings are identical.  Due to some design issues, a dual
Pentium 200 is not reliable, but a dual Pentium 166 is with the
54-24490 card.  Of course, a dual CPU makes no sense unless the
operating system supports it, e.g. NT or Linux.

I have PowerGrade upgrade kits, processors, and processor cards in
stock at reasonable prices.  A Pentium 200 carries a very VERY high
street price right now, so I don't have any available, unless you want
to pay ridiculously large bucks.

The PowerGrade kits for the DECpc XL include a newer and more modern
looking Celebris XL plastic front panel... Ben 

