Ewald,

I have successfully adapted a Toshiba 2X CD-ROM model CR-503 for use
with the 3100 M38. I ripped out the scsi floppy drive, popped the front
face plate off, and plugged it in. You have to reset one of the jumpers
to enable 512 byte sectoring.  I've also plugged in a 364MB IBM scsi
hard drive with good results. The 3100 M38 has a built in ethernet
connection that should work okay on a 10-T LAN.

As for monitors, I think you are on your own when it comes to that. The
system uses a fixed-frequency, sync-on-green system I believe. I'm
