I don't think we are really that far apart - I was looking at
the specifics of running the same compiler on each system  
(the .gcc portion of the specmark itself) and you are, for 
some reason focusing on the native compiler.

This suprises me, because, in my limited experience, native
compilers vary rather drastically in speed and quality.  And
with IBM, you have had even different families of compilers
to choose from (since a compiler isn't bundled anymore).  Thus,
making comparisons of systems by how long it takes to build
the benchmark with a native compiler only gives you more 
information *if you are going to be a developer using the
nativ compiler*.

Nothing beats testing the sytems in the mode you would use them,
but it still seems to me that the SPECint seems a reaonable
comparator (unless, of course, you are doing something math
intesive).

Just my opinion, of course.




