First off, try moving over to comp.os.vms, you will get much better VMS
specific info.
Secondly, all you need is a Null modem cable (ie: with pins 3,2 crossed) and
some simple transfer software. There are versions of Z-modem, and Kermit
available for VMS which will allow you to move (all be it slowly) data from
one system to another.

What you really need to look at  is what information you are thinking of
moving, VMS has a much more complex file structure than Windows/Unix (eg:
ISAM's, VFC...), and there are data types that may cause difficulties (eg:
VAX floating point, or VMS's 8byte internal data/time format, which although
copied by NT has a different starting point). So you may need to do some
file/data conversions before attempting to moving information off of the
VAX.

Laurence.

