I would recommend using ABS. SLS is an older application that requires the
user to write and manage a LOT of .COM files to do what you want.
ABS is the proposed replacement for SLS, and it has a much nicer (i.e.,
simpler)
interface, and is MUCH, MUCH easier to install and set up.
    They're both pretty complete, but some of the more arcane features that
SLS has
are not implemented in ABS...  Configuring ABS to do what you want will be
much
easier than figuring everything out for yourself, then writing .COM files
to do it...

Joe

