As I don't understand your question, I'm just guessing.
You want to configure the DECserver. And you have connected the Ethernet
Interface of the server to your network. And what to do next ? Right ?

Or you did connect the server to the network, loaded it via flash or MOP,
accessed it remotely via MOP, configured server internet characteristics
(IP address, gateway) and now you have problems with the port configurations ?

Or what ? Please give more details.

>                   The terminals connected to the machine (VT510), are well
>configured as the server, but it doesn't prompt anything nor the Digital
>Equipment Corp. login screen, but all terminals Vt510 are configured in
>LOCAL mode, but the screen don't echo anything, and I can't understanding.

The VT510 are well configured ?

What do you mean with LOCAL mode ? Local mode of a VT510 means that
everything you type on the keyboard is displayed on the screen, and
nothing is sent to or received by the serial line interface of the VT510.
This is NOT what you want.

Local Echo mode of a VT510 means that everything you type on the keyboard
is sent to the serial line interface and typed to the screen and everything
received by the serial line interface is typed to the screen.
I bet this is also NOT what you want.

A DECserver 90M config DEFINE PORT all ACCESS LOCAL is maybe what you want,
if you want to use the VT510 to connect over LAT or TELNET to the network
via the DECserver 90M.


The "DigitalEquipment Corp. login screen" is also not clear. Do you mean
the Welcome message of the DECserver:

  Network Access SW V2.3A for DS90M  (BL47-60)

  (c) Copyright 1998, Digital Equipment Corporation - All Rights Reserved

  Please type HELP if you need assistance

  Enter username>

or do you mean the OpenVMS SYS$ANNOUNCE message ?


The OpenVMS announce message is only displayed if
a) the DECserver 90M and the VT510 are properly configured and connected
b) the VMS system is up and reachable
c) the DECserver 90M Port Characteristics are set to a DEDICATED SERVICE.

I think you mean the DECserver Login Screen and this is only displayed if
a) the DECserver 90M is properly configured (PORT: SPEED, ACCESS LOCAL, ...)
b) the VT510 is properly configured (online, speed, ...)
c) the cable is correct (eg. a 6wire DEC423 cable with an H8584-AA adapter)

>        I'm verry worried about that because I ought to finish it now,
>unless my bosses will kill me.Please HELP.

How about beeing more specific in your questions and RTFM ?

